      "notes": "Returns bounded entry and history metadata pages by default; immutable bodies, reusable references and exact selections only when requested. Every result carries the record's 16-hex source_digest, usable for CAS; returned calls pin version, offsets and that digest. Default pages target 2,048 bytes; an explicit body length up to 8,192 scalars returns the largest exact range fitting one 8,192-byte result. This route owns the entry read grammar; workspace_read_page reaches the same owner through entry:{...} and re-addresses the emitted calls to itself.",
