      "notes": "Write-capable agent-safe MCP route for closure updates on a WK or slice. Writes schema-owned closure fields (summary, validation, follow_ups) through validated persistence; caller filesystem roots refuse, as does a malformed or stale expected_source_digest, answered before the request is classified. The explicit optional status done composes authored closure and that transition into one validated canonical write, or persists neither; omitted, closure is recorded without changing status. Completion is never inferred from prose; under DEC-0177 it is not refused for completion_policy forge_confirmed_merge. A mutation that changes canonical bytes runs the generated-view and lint checks once through generateAndLint, reporting a failing check as failing and an unavailable one as not run with its cause, never as a rollback. An unchanged request runs none. When its findings exceed the bounded answer, the complete receipt is retained once and root next_calls reads its findings through workspace_work_record_summary without repeating the write or checks; lint results are repository-scoped (lint_scope repository).",
